# pal-chat-agent.pal - the first real meta-orchestration script (direct
# user ask, 2026-07-20: "a new dir 'pal-scripts/' and running pal-chat-
# agent.pal will navigate to and start the muchi-pal-agent, and start
# the irc-agent-0000 script within the agent" - CHAT-INTEGRATION-
# ARCHITECTURE.txt sec. 6's own planned "llm scripts/ folder", now
# real). Deliberately thin: prisc+x bytecode has no session-management
# opcodes of its own (mkdir/symlink/backgrounding a process aren't
# things li/beq/j can express), so this script's only real job is
# `exec`ing the actual orchestration logic, matching this whole
# family's own op-calls-op convention. See launch_irc_agent.sh's own
# header comment for what actually happens: launches a real, session-
# isolated muchi-pal-agent instance (renderer + chtpm_parser_pal only,
# no keyboard_input - a bot, not a human), then injects "/irc-agent
# <room>" + Enter into it, same technique this whole project was
# hand-verified with all session. Set $IRC_ROOM before running this
# script to pick a room other than the "general" default (exec's own
# system() call inherits prisc+x's full environment automatically - no
# pal-level string-passing needed, `exec` can only pass INTEGER args
# via registers, never arbitrary text, so this is the only clean way
# to hand a room name through).
#
# Usage: IRC_ROOM=<room> ./system/prisc+x pal-chat-agent.pal
exec ./launch_irc_agent.sh
halt
